1. She is from England. (Verbatim: "It's only like from England. 10 hour flight.")
2. She has an iron bladder and can hold her urine for long periods during flights. (Verbatim: "I can confirm as I do on all long-haul flights, I didn't get up once to go bathroom.")
3. She dislikes aisle seats on airplanes and prefers window seats. (Verbatim: "personally, personally I like the window seat.")
4. She experiences anxiety about getting up and moving on planes. (Verbatim: "Getting up on a plane, walking over to the bathroom, just makes me anxious.")
5. She strongly dislikes American Coca-Cola due to its high fructose corn syrup. (Verbatim: "It was full of high fructose corn syrup. Absolutely, truly upsetting.")
6. She enjoys sour cream flavored mini pretzels served on certain flights. (Verbatim: "they're like sour cream flavored pretzels, and they're these little tiny ones, and it's a really good snack.")
7. She likes playing Fire Emblem games, specifically restarted Fire Emblem: Three Houses and chose the white-haired female route. (Verbatim: "I restarted Fire Emblem: Three Heroes... I picked the white-haired lady.")
8. She has attended Anime Expo in Los Angeles, California, multiple times. (Verbatim: "So I had to, first off, fly... to Anime Expo.")
9. She flew to the U.S. for Anime Expo and went through customs, which was less intense on her second visit. (Verbatim: "This time I got asked like two questions... What you visiting for? And I was like, Anime Expo.")
10. She previously had her luggage inspected by the TSA during a past trip to America. (Verbatim: "I opened up my suitcase and it had the little note being like, The TSA have inspected this bag.") [end of text]



1. She refers to her personal sense of time as "Ellia land," indicating she often has an irregular sleep schedule due to jet lag and time zone differences. (Verbatim: "I'm in my own time zone, I live in Ellia land, Ellia land is where I live.")

2. She has experienced significant jet lag when traveling between America and England, which disrupts her sleeping pattern. (Verbatim: "I just feel like waking up at like 2pm... waking up at 2pm in America doesn't equal waking up at a normal time in England either.")

3. She attended Anime Expo and arrived early to adjust to jet lag before the event. (Verbatim: "I arrived a little before Anime Expo, just so I could adjust my jet lag.")

4. She helped a friend set up their booth at Anime Expo on the day before the event opened. (Verbatim: "I went on the Wednesday where they were still setting up everything... I was helping out a friend with her booth and helping her carry some stuff in.")

5. She has a particular fondness for Artist Alley at conventions, calling it the "bane of my wallet" due to her love of artist merchandise. (Verbatim: "Artist Alley is the hall where you have all the artists and that's where you find all the cute merch... aka the bane of my wallet.")

6. She cosplayed as Yor from *Spy x Family* at Anime Expo, with Mozzy doing the color edit over her photos. (Verbatim: "I cosplayed as yor from spy family yeah mozzy did the did the color over and stuff.")

7. She revealed her real body in a photo, confirming that while her head was chibi-styled, her body proportions are real. (Verbatim: "This is actually my body... those are my arms that's my thigh.")

8. She wears UK size 4 shoes and describes her feet as tiny. (Verbatim: "these are uk size four... i also have tiny feet.")

9. She finds high heels difficult to walk in and experienced foot pain after wearing them all day at the convention. (Verbatim: "my feet were hurting by the end of the day... they're heckin difficult to walk around in.")

10. She humorously claims to "live offline" and not exist on social media when asked by fans at the convention. (Verbatim: "i live offline i do not exist... what is what is social.") [end of text]



